ks worldwide (FWCI 1 = world average).","Above the world average: 0%–10% of the works per year have an FWCI above 1, most in 2018 (10%).","Not cited: on average 83% of these works have FWCI 0, meaning no citations within their four-year window. That is why many boxes start at 0.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 5 of 8 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2018: mean 0.6, median 0.35, top work 2.63. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Still counting: works from 2023 have not completed their four-year citation window, so their values will rise. Do not compare them with older years yet.","Small base: the values for 2006–2012, 2018 and 2023 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2004–2005, 2014, 2017, 2019–2022 and 2024–2026 have fewer than 10 works, too few for a box. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."],"citations":["Typical work: works published 2006–2023 have a median of 0–5 citations each; the highest median (5) is in 2011.","Most cited works: the top 10% of works published in 2012 have at least 12.4 citations each, the highest P90 in the chart.","Not yet cited: more than half of the works published 2023 have no citations so far. This is expected for recent works and is not a sign of low quality.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 7 of 9 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2018: mean 5.3, median 3, top work 17. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Small base: the values for 2006–2012, 2018 and 2023 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2004–2005, 2014, 2017, 2019–2022 and 2024–2026 have fewer than 10 works, too few for a band. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."]}}}